  "enable": "Control over the network needs the unit control source set to Network at the keypad (Main Menu > Ctrl Source = Network; default Local). NetworkCtrl (MV 24562) then commands Off/On/Ventilation/Economy/Scheduler and SuWiNetworkChgover (MV 28594) sets cool or heat.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "BACnet IP comes from a POL908 module and BACnet MS/TP from a POL904 module on the AHU controller.",
   "Module settings are under Commissioning > Communication > Comm modules on the unit display; the module BUS LED must be green.",
   "BACnet IP: DHCP is on by default, UDP port 47808; after changing addresses set Apply Changes = Yes, which restarts the controller.",
   "BACnet MS/TP: MAC address 24, 38400 baud, Max Master 127, Max Info Frames 1; cycle power after changing the MAC. The termination resistor setting must be Yes only on the first and last unit.",
   "Device instance and object name are derived from the module (MAC address for IP, production number for MS/TP)."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Objects only appear when the AHU configuration uses them.",
   "GlblAlrmSwtc (BO 48570) reads 1 when any alarm is active; AlmCl0-3 (MV 46769, 42640, 38643, 34514) show alarms by class.",
   "Every setpoint AV here is writable, including defrost and pre-heating settings; only write the operating setpoints from the BMS."
  ]
 },
